/E (The drive system is responsible for converting electrical energy from the battery into mechanical motion to move the vehicle. It mainly consists of a BLDC motor and motor controller. The motor controller receives commands from the VCU and regulates the motor speed and torque based on driver input and operating conditions. The BLDC motor provides high efficiency, smooth operation, and low maintenance. The system also supports features like speed control, torque control, and regenerative braking, improving overall performance and energy efficiency.)
